{
    "background_story": "Tommy was a young anthropologist who had always been fascinated by the cultures of Africa. During his research, he stumbled upon the Umbundu people, an ethnic group from Angola. He became captivated by their rich traditions and decided to embark on a journey to learn more. Tommy spent several months living among the Umbundu, immersing himself in their customs and language. He was particularly drawn to their vibrant music and dance, often joining in during celebrations. As he delved deeper into their culture, Tommy discovered a sense of community and belonging he had never experienced before. He eventually wrote a book about his experiences, shedding light on the beauty and resilience of the Umbundu people. Tommy's adventure not only broadened his perspective but also forged unbreakable bonds with his new Umbundu friends.",
